{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "ProxyPics API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The ProxyPics API allows you to programatically manage your photo requests inside ProxyPics.\n\nThe API exposes REST endpoints that exclusively speak JSON format.\n\n## API Endpoints\n\nLive API: `https://api.proxypics.com/api/v3`\n\nFor testing your integration, we have a sandbox environment, it is another instance of ProxyPics platform. All requests created under the sandbox aren't available for anyone to complete them, so we have some tools that will allow you to simulate photos submission, photos approval or rejection.\n\nSandbox endpoint: `https://sandbox.proxypics.com/api/v3`\n\nSandbox web app: `https://sandbox-app.proxypics.com`\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery request to ProxyPics API is authenticated with an API Key.\n\nYou can generate an API Key by going to your Profile page, Integrations left tab here: `https://app.proxypics.com/profile`.\nIn this page you can generate new API Keys as well as configure your webhooks.\n\nYou can pass the API Key either in a header property called `x-api-key` or by the query parameter `api_key`.\n\n## Testing your integration\n\nAs said before we have a sandbox instance of ProxyPics platform running on `https://sandbox-app.proxypics.com`.\n\nTo start testing your integration create an account at https://sandbox-app.proxypics.com, setup an API Key and start integrating against the sandbox endpoint (`https://sandbox.proxypics.com`).\n\nIn order to successfuly create requests, you'll need to add a credit card. You can use the number `4111 1111 1111 1111` with any CVV and a future expiration date.\n\n## Pagination\n\nEvery collection endpoints are paginated. The resources are returned inside a `data` key and the pagination meta data is returned inside the `meta.pagination` object.\n\nExample:\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": { \"...\": \"...\" },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"pagination\": {\n      \"total\": 45,\n      \"current_page\": 1,\n      \"per_page\": 10\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Content-Type\n\nAll requests made to the API should have the Content-Type equals to `application/json`.\n\n## Errors\n\nErrors will be returned with HTTP codes 400, 401, 404 and 422. The response has an `errors` key with a list of the errors occurred.\n\nExample:\n```json\n{\n  \"errors\": [ ... ]\n}\n```\n\n## Event Types\n\nEvery time you receive a webhook, there's a \"event_name\" attribute that identifies the event name.\n\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestAdded\"` -> Photo request created\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestUnassigned\"` -> Photo request unassigned, waiting for a data collector\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestAssigned\"` -> Photo request assigned to a Data Collector\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestUploadStarted\"` -> DC started to take pictures\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::AppointmentScheduled\"` -> Appointment scheduled\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::AwaitingSignatures\"` -> Awaiting signatures, 1004D Alternative\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::SignatureCollected\"` -> Signature collected, 1004D Alternative\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestCanceled\"` -> Photo request canceled\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestCompleted\"` -> Photo request completed, still waiting for review.\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestExpired\"` -> Photo request expired, rarely happens\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestOnHold\"` -> Photo request put on hold\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PaymentProcessing::PhotoRequestCostUpdated\"` -> Fee updated\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestReportGenerated\"` -> Sent with the \u201cfulfilled\u201d status, the report is ready to be downloaded\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestResumed\"` -> Removed from hold\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::WebAppOpened\"` -> Web App opened by the POC, Direct orders\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PocTextMessageSent\"` -> Text message sent to the POC, Direct orders\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestTemplateChanged\"` -> When the template is changed in the order\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::PhotoDelivery::PhotoRequestExpirationChanged\"` -> When expiration time of the order is changed\n- `\"ProxyPicsEvents::Messaging::MessageAdded\"` -> Message added to an order by the ProxyPics team\n",
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://api.swaggerhub.com/apis/proxypics/proxypics-api/1.0.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.proxypics.com/api/v3",
      "description": "Live API"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://sandbox.proxypics.com/api/v3",
      "description": "Sandbox API"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Photo Requests",
      "description": "The photo request is the main object in the ProxyPics platform. It is created by you, the requester,\nand will have all the info that describes your request.\n\nBasically a photo task is made of an **Address**, **Tasks** (the defined photos the user should take),\n**Unlimited Tasks** (extra photos the user can freely take), **Question Groups**\n(groups of questions the user should answer).\n\nProxyPics has two different platforms: ProxyPics Crowdsource and ProxyPics Direct.\n\n#### ProxyPics Crowdsource\nPhoto requests in the Crowdsource platform will be available for any photo taker from our users base to pick up the request for completion.\n\n#### ProxyPics Direct\nDirect requests are directly assigned to someone by his phone number and then an SMS will be sent with instructions for completing the photo request.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "UPD/PDR/PDC",
      "description": "To create a UPD order, use the /photo-requests POST endpoint and just provide the address and UPD fields\ninside \"uniform_property_dataset_report_attributes\".\n\nThe UPD template is automatically chosen by the system, you don't need to submit the \"template_token\" field for UPDs.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Photo Request Templates / Products",
      "description": "Photo Request Templates (Products) allows you to reuse the shape of a photo request across different photo requests."
    },
    {
      "name": "Appraisal Requests",
      "description": "Appraisal requests and photo requests are two different things. If you want an appraisal request with up to date photos,\nyou need to first create the appraisal request and later create the photo request passing the appraisal request id.\n\nThere are three different appraisal requests available through the API: AVMs, simple BPOs and BPOs with adjustments.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "API Keys",
      "description": "You can manage your api keys within our API."
    },
    {
      "name": "Companies",
      "description": "Update company account and set notification types you want to subscribe."
    },
    {
      "name": "Webhooks",
      "description": "Whenever there are changes on any ProxyPics resource, it triggers a `GET` or `POST` request to an URL you've configured\nin the Integration section of your Company profile in the ProxyPics platform.\n\nIf you choose to create a `GET` Webhook, the query for this request will have two params, `resource_type`\n(PhotoRequest or AppraisalRequest) and `resource_id` and you can use it to fetch the resource from the API and act accordingly.\n\nIf you choose to create a `POST` Webhook, the body for this request will have all the resource attributes (PhotoRequest or AppraisalRequest).\n\nYou can also set a `username` and a `password` for HTTP Basic authentication.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Messages",
      "description": "You can send API notes (messages) to a Photo Request.\nA webhook will be triggered when ProxyPics sends a message to any of your Photo Requests.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "CSV Uploads",
      "description": "You can list and get a single CSV Upload from your company."
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "ApiKeyHeader": []
    },
    {
      "ApiKeyQuery": []
    }
  ],
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "ApiKeyHeader": {
        "type": "apiKey",
        "in": "header",
        "name": "x-api-key",
        "description": "API key authentication via `x-api-key` header."
      },
      "ApiKeyQuery": {
        "type": "apiKey",
        "in": "query",
        "name": "api_key",
        "description": "API key authentication via `api_key` query parameter."
      }
    },
    "parameters": {
      "PageParam": {
        "name": "page",
        "in": "query",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "type": "integer",
          "default": 1
        }
      },
      "PerPageParam": {
        "name": "per_page",
        "in": "query",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "type": "integer",
          "default": 10
        }
      },
      "IdPathParamInteger": {
        "name": "id",
        "in": "path",
        "required": true,
        "schema": {
          "type": "integer"
        }
      }
    },
    "responses": {
      "Error400": {
        "description": "Bad Request",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "Error401": {
        "description": "Unauthorized",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "Error404": {
        "description": "Not Found",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "Error422": {
        "description": "Unprocessable Entity",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
